# TRAX AI Memory System

You have persistent memory at ~/Obsidian Brain/claude-brain/

At session start, ALWAYS:
1. Read ~/Obsidian Brain/claude-brain/memory/hot.md (last session summary)
2. Read ~/Obsidian Brain/claude-brain/MEMORY.md (full note index)
3. Load relevant notes from ~/Obsidian Brain/claude-brain/memory/ based on what's being worked on

At session end, ALWAYS:
1. Update hot.md with a compact summary
2. Create or update relevant notes in memory/
3. Update MEMORY.md if notes were added or removed

Note organization: project_*.md, client_*.md, decisions_*.md, prefs_*.md, reference_*.md
Use [[wikilinks]] for cross-references.

About TRAX: AI agency (Antwerp + Paris). Sam = commercial, Taddeo = technical.
Three pillars: Audit, Train, Build. Check memory notes for full context.
